 "marks": [
  {
   "d": "2022-01-27",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "These conditions have continued into the second half of the year and as a result we remain optimistic about prospects although we expect the rate of growth to slow as the economy gradually returns to normal.",
   "file": "20220127_CFX_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-04-21",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 2,
   "q": "Fabric Division profitability is highly operationally geared and as a result of higher than expected sales the Board now expects the Group's profits before tax for the year ended 30 April 2022 to be ahead of market expectations.",
   "file": "20220421_CFX_Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-08-17",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Rising interest rates and high levels of inflation have already started to slow housing market activity and we are therefore cautious about prospects for the coming year especially as we tend to lag changes in the housing market.",
   "file": "20220817_CFX_Preliminary-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-09-29",
   "doc": "AGM",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "We have just entered our important autumn selling season and as previously reported we are expecting trading conditions to become more challenging in the second half of the year.",
   "file": "20220929_CFX_AGM-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-01-23",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "In addition we benefitted from a very strong US Dollar exchange rate and as a result, we now expect our full year performance to 30 April 2023 to be ahead of previous expectations.",
   "file": "20230123_CFX_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-08-09",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "The performance of our core Fabric Division lags activity in the high-end housing market and we do expect trading conditions to become progressively more challenging as steep interest rate increases start to have an impact in the US and the UK. These expectations are factored into our current year market forecast.",
   "file": "20230809_CFX_Final-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-09-28",
   "doc": "AGM",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "We have just entered our important autumn selling season and as reported when we announced our year end results, we are expecting trading conditions to become progressively more challenging due to the adverse impact of high interest rates on housing transactions and home spending.",
   "file": "20230928_CFX_AGM-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-01-30",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "The Group has delivered a good performance in the first six months which is broadly in line with expectations and follows record interim profits in the prior year.",
   "file": "20240130_CFX_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-07-31",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Over the last year higher interest rates have reduced housing market activity and we are expecting difficult market conditions in the year ahead and this is reflected in our existing market forecast.",
   "file": "20240731_CFX_Preliminary-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-09-26",
   "doc": "AGM",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The sales performance in the US is slightly better than we expected at the start of the year but the benefit will be offset by a significantly weaker US dollar exchange rate. Overall we expect the Group's performance for the financial year to remain in line with market expectations.",
   "file": "20240926_CFX_AGM-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-01-22",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Market conditions in the UK and Europe are currently challenging and we expect these conditions to continue through the second half of the year.",
   "file": "20250122_CFX_Half-year-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-07-29",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY26",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -3,
   "q": "Whilst our core Fabric Division business continues to perform well, we remain cautious about prospects and in particular the impact of higher tariff costs, a weaker US Dollar and lower Decorating Division profits",
